New skills for making and improving gear.

 - Smelt (warrior): melt metal items and ore down into ingots.
 - Forge (warrior): make armor and weapons from ingots.
 - Weave (monk): unravel cloth and leather into thread.
 - Sew (monk): make clothing and light armor from thread.
 - Strip (thief): cut armor down a tier so more classes can wear it.
 - Plate (deikhan): build armor up a tier for more protection.
 - Transmute (mage): change what an item is made of.
 - Distill (mage): break jewelry down into essences.
 - Infuse (mage): add an essence's stat to a piece of gear.
 - Bangle (shaman): turn gear into jewelry any class can wear.
 - Ensoul (shaman): make a soulstone from an opal.
 - Rites (cleric): draw a corpse's soul into a soulstone.
 - Mine (adventuring): dig ore out of hills, mountains and caves.
 - Tailor (adventuring): resize clothing for another race.
 - Bolster (adventuring): improve armor using a soulstone.

TNT now sets off other armed traps, and blasting rock frees ore.

